          ],
          "interaction": {
            "kind": "speaking",
            "prompt": [
              {
                "t": "text",
                "v": "Look at the photograph of people on bicycles and talk about it on your own for about one minute."
              }
            ],
            "turns": [
              {
                "id": "t1",
                "text": "Now I’d like you to talk on your own about something. I’m going to give you a photograph and I’d like you to talk about it. Here is your photograph. It shows people on bicycles. Please tell us what you can see in the photograph.",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t2-s-q2-t1.mp3",
                  "seconds": 17.5
                }
              }
            ],
            "maxSeconds": 75,
            "scoring": "judge"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "part": 3,
      "label": "Part 3",
      "instruction": "Talk together with your partner about the situation.",
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "q3",
          "number": 3,
          "points": 20,
          "skills": [],
          "material": [
            {
              "id": "i2",
              "type": "imageRef",
              "image": "img2"
            }
          ],
          "interaction": {
            "kind": "speaking",
            "prompt": [
              {
                "t": "text",
                "v": "Talk with your partner about the different ways a girl could find out about the history of her local area, and decide which would be best."
              }
            ],
            "turns": [
              {
                "id": "t1",
                "text": "Now, in this part of the test you’re going to talk about something together for about two minutes. I’m going to describe a situation to you. A girl is going to write an article for her school magazine about the history of her local area. She wants to find out more about it. Here are some ways she could find out about the history of her local area. Talk together about the different ways she could find out about the history of the local area and say which would be best. All right? Now, talk together.",
                "role": "examiner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t2-s-q3-t1.mp3",
                  "seconds": 37
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t2",
                "text": "Shall I start? I think talking to an old person is a great idea. They can tell her real stories about the past. What do you think?",
                "role": "partner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t2-s-q3-t2.mp3",
                  "seconds": 8.6
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t3",
                "text": "That’s true. What about looking on the internet? It’s quick and easy, but is the information always correct?",
                "role": "partner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t2-s-q3-t3.mp3",
                  "seconds": 6.8
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t4",
                "text": "I like the idea of a museum too, because she can see old things from her area. Do you agree?",
                "role": "partner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t2-s-q3-t4.mp3",
                  "seconds": 5.9
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t5",
                "text": "And what about a guided tour of the castle? The guide knows a lot, but it might be expensive. What’s your opinion?",
                "role": "partner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t2-s-q3-t5.mp3",
                  "seconds": 7.2
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t6",
                "text": "She could also look at old maps and books, or read the sign on the statue. Are those useful, do you think?",
                "role": "partner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t2-s-q3-t6.mp3",
                  "seconds": 6.9
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t7",
                "text": "So, which way do you think would be best for her article? I think talking to an old person, because her story would be really interesting.",
                "role": "partner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t2-s-q3-t7.mp3",
                  "seconds": 8
                }
              }
            ],
            "maxSeconds": 45,
            "scoring": "judge"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "part": 4,
      "label": "Part 4",
      "instruction": "Answer the examiner’s questions about the topic of Part 3.",
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "q4",
          "number": 4,
          "points": 20,
          "skills": [],
          "interaction": {
            "kind": "speaking",
            "prompt": [
              {
                "t": "text",
                "v": "Answer the examiner’s questions about history and learning about the past."
              }
            ],
            "turns": [
              {
                "id": "t1",
                "text": "Do you like learning about history at school? Why? / Why not?",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t2-s-q4-t1.mp3",
                  "seconds": 5.7
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t2",
                "text": "Have you been on a school trip to a museum? What did you see?",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t2-s-q4-t2.mp3",
                  "seconds": 4.8
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t3",
                "text": "Do you enjoy watching films about the past? Why? / Why not?",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t2-s-q4-t3.mp3",
                  "seconds": 6
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t4",
                "text": "Is it interesting to visit historical buildings like castles? Why? / Why not?",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t2-s-q4-t4.mp3",
                  "seconds": 6.8
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t5",
                "text": "Do you think it’s important for young people to learn about the past? Why? / Why not?",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t2-s-q4-t5.mp3",
                  "seconds": 6.8
                }
              }
            ],
            "maxSeconds": 40,
            "scoring": "judge"
          }
        }
      ]
